slop — a linter and code-structure query tool
Copyright 2025 Jordan Godau

slop implements established software metrics from the published work listed
below. The metrics are formulas computed from source structure; slop implements
them independently via tree-sitter AST traversal. No code from the original
authors' implementations is used.

The codebase (src/slop/) is original work by the author, licensed under the
Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE). It contains no third-party code.

MEASURES
========

Cyclomatic Complexity (cyclomatic-complexity)
  McCabe, T.J. (1976). "A Complexity Measure." IEEE Transactions on
  Software Engineering, SE-2(4), 308-320.

Cognitive Complexity (cognitive-complexity)
  Campbell, G.A. (2018). "Cognitive Complexity: A new way of measuring
  understandability." SonarSource SA. Technical report.

NPath (npath-complexity)
  Nejmeh, B.A. (1988). "NPATH: A Measure of Execution Path Complexity and
  its Applications." Communications of the ACM, 31(2), 188-200.

Chidamber & Kemerer Object-Oriented Metrics (class-coupling, class-inheritance-depth, class-children)
  Chidamber, S.R. & Kemerer, C.F. (1994). "A Metrics Suite for Object
  Oriented Design." IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering, 20(6),
  476-493.

  Metrics implemented: CBO (Coupling Between Object Classes), DIT (Depth
  of Inheritance Tree), NOC (Number of Children).

Cohesion, LCOM4 (class-cohesion, off by default; slop shape)
  Hitz, M. & Montazeri, B. (1995). "Measuring Coupling and Cohesion in
  Object-Oriented Systems." Institut fuer Angewandte Informatik und
  Systemanalyse, University of Vienna.

  Metric implemented: LCOM4, the number of connected components of the
  graph joining a class's methods through the instance members they share
  or call. Methods reaching no instance member are reported as detached.

Distance from the Main Sequence (rigid-package, useless-package)
  Martin, R.C. (1994). "OO Design Quality Metrics: An Analysis of
  Dependencies." Proceedings of Workshop Pragmatic and Theoretical
  Directions in Object-Oriented Software Metrics, OOPSLA '94.

  Martin, R.C. (2002). "Agile Software Development: Principles, Patterns,
  and Practices." Prentice Hall. Chapter 20: Principles of Package Design.

  Metrics implemented: Instability (I), Abstractness (A), Distance from
  the Main Sequence (D').

Hotspot Analysis (slop hotspots)
  Tornhill, A. (2015). "Your Code as a Crime Scene." Pragmatic Bookshelf.

Software Science (halstead-volume)
  Halstead, M.H. (1977). "Elements of Software Science." Elsevier.

Magic numbers (magic-literal)
  Martin, R.C. (2008). "Clean Code: A Handbook of Agile Software Craftsmanship."
  Prentice Hall. G25: Replace Magic Numbers with Named Constants.
  Fowler, M. (1999). "Refactoring: Improving the Design of Existing Code."
  Addison-Wesley. Replace Magic Number with Symbolic Constant.

Acyclic Dependencies Principle (import-cycle)
  Lakos, J. (1996). "Large-Scale C++ Software Design." Addison-Wesley.
  Tarjan, R.E. (1972). "Depth-First Search and Linear Graph Algorithms."
  SIAM Journal on Computing, 1(2), 146-160. (Strongly connected components.)

Identifier noise list (lexicon)
  Newman, C.D., AlSuhaibani, R.S., Collard, M.L. & Maletic, J.I. (2017).
  "Lexical Categories for Source Code Identifiers." 24th IEEE International
  Conference on Software Analysis, Evolution and Reengineering (SANER 2017),
  228-237. slop's STOP_WORDS contains the 14 identifiers the authors found
  common to all 50 C/C++ systems they studied.
